❓ Troubleshooting
    1. No module named ...
     Re-install the required packages using:
     Bash
      python -m pip install -r requirements.txt

   2. InvalidToken Error
     Make sure you set the token correctly in your environment before running the bot:

    DOS
     set TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=YOUR_BOT_TOKEN
     python bot.py

   3. requirements.txt not found
     Ensure you are inside the correct project directory:

    Bash
     cd Insta-Reel-Downloader-Telegram-Bot
     python -m pip install -r requirements.txt

🔒 Security
      Never hardcode your Telegram Bot Token directly inside bot.py or any source code file.
      Always use the environment variable TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN.
      If your token is accidentally leaked or pushed to GitHub, revoke and regenerate it immediately via BotFather.

⚠️ Limitations
      Instagram platform updates may affect downloader availability.
      Private accounts, deleted posts, restricted media, or region-locked content cannot be downloaded.
      Successful downloads depend on the public accessibility of the link.

